# Education investment share and per-capita output: LMC vs Sub-Saharan Africa
ASSOCIATIONAL analysis only. Staged file only; N=2 aggregate units x T=41 years.

## Corrections to the brief (documented, not errors in execution)
| Brief says | Data actually contains |
|---|---|
| per capita GDP, 2010 US$ | GNI per capita, constant 2015 US$ (NY.GNP.PCAP.KD) |
| govt education expenditure, % of total expenditure | Adjusted savings: education expenditure, % of GNI (NY.ADJ.AEDU.GN.ZS) |
| panel of countries | 2 WDI aggregate groups (LMC, SSA); no country-level rows |

## Data
12 rows x 45 cols; 41 year columns 1975-2015; 84/492 cells empty.
Coverage: SSA GNIpc n=5 (2011-15 only!) -> only 4 annual growth changes; LMC GNIpc n=41;
LFPR n=25 both (1991-15); SSA export growth n=25 (1991-15); edu share and both GERs n=41 both.

